.nh
.TH "AEGIS" "1" "May 2026" "aegis 0.1.0-demo" "Aegis Manual"

.SH NAME
aegis-explain - Show why a dep was flagged — capability descriptions + risk breakdown + evidence


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBaegis explain  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
explain looks up the dep in the saved aegis.lock first (no network).
If not found, falls back to a fresh fetch + AST scan.

.PP
Each capability is shown with a one-line human description; flags
include the suppression reason when allowlisted; evidence (file:line
snippets) is shown when the scan was fresh.

.PP
Examples:
  aegis explain lodash@4.17.21
  aegis explain @solana/web3.js@1.95.4
  aegis explain --snapshot-only ua-parser-js@0.7.29   # error if not in lock


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for explain

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	emit machine-readable JSON to stdout

.PP
\fB--snapshot-only\fP[=false]
	only consult the saved aegis.lock; never fetch + rescan


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	enable debug-level structured logging to stderr


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBaegis(1)\fP
